-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_58.sql (Isaiah 58) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 58 — THE TRUE FAST + ★THE SABBATH A DELIGHT, the anti-antinomian chapter and
-- a framework keystone. The empty ritual fast is rebuked (*Wherefore have we fasted, say they,
-- and thou seest not?... in the day of your fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours*,
-- 58:3) — fasting while oppressing is no fast at all (Zechariah 7:5-6 the same lawsuit; Matthew
-- 6:16-18 the fast not for show; Sirach 34:25-26 the man that fasteth for his sins and goes again
-- and doeth the same). NOT the abolition of fasting — the exposure of heartless ritual divorced
-- from justice. The TRUE fast is covenant-mercy: *to loose the bands of wickedness... to deal thy
-- bread to the hungry... that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh* (58:6-7) — the very
-- works of Matthew 25:35-36 (*I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat*), the pure religion of James
-- 1:27 / the living faith of James 2:15-16, the Torah-mercy of Deuteronomy 15:7-11. The obedient
-- are blessed with restoration: *thy light break forth as the morning... thou shalt be called,
-- The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in* (58:8,12 — Matthew 5:14-16 the
-- light; Amos 9:11 the breaches closed, the tabernacle of David raised). And the climax, the
-- anti-antinomian KEYSTONE: *call the sabbath a delight, the holy of Yahuah, honourable... then
-- shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah... and feed thee with the heritage of Jacob thy father*
-- (58:13-14) — the Sabbath KEPT and called a DELIGHT, never abolished, never a burden (Exodus
-- 20:8-11; Mark 2:27-28 made for man, the Son of Adam Lord of the sabbath — kept not cancelled;
-- Isaiah 56:2 the man that keepeth the sabbath; Hebrews 4:9 the rest that remaineth; the 1 John
-- 2:3-4 obedience filter). The heritage of Jacob = the two-house covenant inheritance.
-- Tag: isa58   Temp view: _s303_isa58_lookup
-- Sort band: base 27425, step 3 -> threads at 27425, 27428, 27431, 27434, 27437, 27440, 27443 (7 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',58,v
--
-- Isaiah 58 coverage:
--   ★★ v.1-5 (Wherefore have we fasted, say they, and thou seest not?... in the day of your fast
--          ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours... ye fast for strife and debate... is it
--          such a fast that I have chosen?)
--        NT:     ★★ Matthew 6:16 (when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance) +
--                Matthew 6:17-18 (anoint thine head... appear not unto men to fast) — THREAD 1
--        Extras: ★★ Sirach 34:26 (So is it with a man that fasteth for his sins, and goes again, and
--                doeth the same: who will hear his prayer?) + Sirach 34:25 — THREAD 1 (extras)
--        Tanakh: ★★ Zechariah 7:5 (When ye fasted and mourned... did ye at all fast unto me?) +
--                Zechariah 7:6 (did ye not eat for yourselves?) — THREAD 1
--   ★★★ v.6 (Is not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the
--          heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke?)
--        NT:     ★★★ Matthew 25:35 (I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat... I was a stranger, and ye
--                took me in) + Matthew 25:36 + Matthew 25:40 (unto the least of these my brethren) — THREAD 2
--        Extras: ★ Sirach 34:21 (bread of the needy is their life) + 34:22 (defraudeth the labourer of
--                his hire is a bloodshedder) — weighed; held in prose / woven w/ THREAD 1 (oppression),
--                not double-added (the true-fast NT witness Matt 25 is the load-bearing fill) — none added
--        Tanakh: ★★ Deuteronomy 15:7 (thou shalt not harden thine heart, nor shut thine hand from thy
--                poor brother) + Deuteronomy 15:11 (open thine hand wide unto thy brother) — THREAD 2
--   ★★★ v.7 (Is it not to deal thy bread to the hungry... when thou seest the naked, that thou cover
--          him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh?)
--        NT:     ★★★ James 2:15 (If a brother or sister be naked, and destitute of daily food) + James
--                2:16 (ye give them not those things which are needful... what doth it profit?) +
--                ★★ James 1:27 (Pure religion... To visit the fatherless and widows) — THREAD 3
--        Extras: none warranted (the doers-of-the-word fill is the NT's own James witness)
--        Tanakh: woven (the bread-to-the-hungry is the Deuteronomy 15 mercy of THREAD 2; in prose)
--   ★★ v.8,10-12 (Then shall thy light break forth as the morning... thou shalt be like a watered
--          garden... thou shalt be called, The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in)
--        NT:     ★★ Matthew 5:14 (Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill) +
--                Matthew 5:16 (Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works) — THREAD 4
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★★ Amos 9:11 (I raise up the tabernacle of David that is fallen, and close up the
--                breaches thereof) — THREAD 4 (the repairer of the breach = the restoration ministry)
--   ★★★ v.13 (call the sabbath a delight, the holy of Yahuah, honourable; and shalt honour him, not
--          doing thine own ways) + ★★★ v.14 (Then shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah... feed thee
--          with the heritage of Jacob thy father)
--        NT:     ★★★ Mark 2:27 (The sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath) + Mark 2:28
--                (the Son of Adam is Yahuah also of the sabbath) + ★★ Hebrews 4:9 (There remaineth
--                therefore a rest to the people of Elohim) + ★ 1 John 2:3 FILTER + 1 John 2:4 — THREAD 5/6
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★★★ Exodus 20:8 (Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy) + Exodus 20:10 + Exodus
--                20:11 (Yahuah blessed the sabbath day, and hallowed it) + ★★ Isaiah 56:2 (the son of
--                Adam... that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it) — THREAD 5
--
-- Threads (slug — target libraries):
